[task-01] A repeated review's judgements must not drift. When a review runs again over
    stored earlier state and judges a criterion for a second time, it works from the
    rating it recorded before and from the changes to that criterion's dependencies
    since then.
    -> repeated-review-judgements-stable  [functional/explicit]
       A repeated review's judgements work from the rating recorded before and from the
       changes to that criterion's dependencies since then.
    -> changed-criterion-uses-stored-rating  [functional/explicit]
       A judgement asked for a criterion that changed is given the rating stored for
       that criterion.
    -> changed-criterion-uses-dependency-changes  [functional/explicit]
       A judgement asked for a criterion that changed is given the changes to that
       criterion's dependencies.
    -> request-includes-rating-and-dependency-changes  [invariant/explicit]
       The stored rating and the dependency changes given to a judgement are part of the
       request that judgement is recorded under.
    -> rating-change-must-name-given-change  [functional/explicit]   (also serves constraint-04)
       A judgement that alters a rating names one of the changes it was given.
    -> rejected-when-no-given-change-named  [error_handling/explicit]
       A judgement that alters a rating while naming no change it was given is rejected
       by the code that reads the judgement, rather than by the instruction that asked
       for it.
    -> rejected-judgement-keeps-stored-rating  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-06)
       A rejected judgement leaves the stored rating in place.
    -> rejected-judgement-is-reported  [explanation_observability/explicit]   (also serves constraint-07, completion-07)
       A rejected judgement is reported.
    -> no-stored-state-judges-without-stored-rating  [functional/explicit]   (also serves constraint-08)
       A review with no stored earlier state judges every criterion without reference to
       any stored rating.
    -> same-state-same-inputs-same-review-state  [regression/explicit]   (also serves constraint-09)
       A review repeated over the same stored state and the same inputs produces the
       same review state as the one before it.

